<h3>Hypothetical widgets</h3>
<p>Some hypotheticals. What if a widget company&#8217;s board met in secret?&#8203; Nobody could do anything about anything.<sup><a href="#footnote-1">[1]</a></sup> So nobody would. &#128578;</p>
<ul><li>The board would meet.</li><li>The board would decide.</li></ul>
<blockquote>Widget Corp. said it was &#8220;considering all options,&#8221; according to people familiar with the matter.</blockquote>
<p>I don&#8217;t know what that means either.</p>
<h3>Procurement</h3>
<p>Anyway, a pretend official steered pretend companies toward a pretend bank.<sup><a href="#footnote-2">[2]</a></sup></p>
<h3>Things happen</h3>
<p>Widgets Are the New Gadgets. A Pretend Bank Hires a Pretend Banker.</p>
<p id="footnote-1">[1] Not formally, but informally, sure.</p>
<p id="footnote-2">[2] Disclosure, I used to work at a pretend bank.</p>
<p>Follow Us</p>
